## Equalize page-title top inset with subtitle gap

Context: Section titles sat flush to the content top on desktop
(``padding-top: 0``) while the subtitle-to-content gap was 0.5rem. Pages
looked tighter above the heading than below it (e.g. "Domain Information").

Changes:

1. `src/front/static/global/css/main.css`
   `.section-header` and `.page-header` top padding is 0.5rem, matching the
   header's bottom margin (subtitle -> content).
2. `src/front/static/global/css/sidebar-layout.css`
   Desktop sidebar titles keep 0.5rem top padding instead of zeroing it.
3. `tests/units/front/test_clarity_design_contract.py`
   Contract: title top inset equals subtitle -> content gap (0.5rem).
4. `.cursor/11-frontend-design.mdc`
   Document the 0.5rem title inset.

